#!/usr/bin/env bash

lord --verbose << "EOF"
Write a script called bin/update-english.

The script should take:

  1. a .tex file or a directory containing .tex files
  2. an eng/ subfolder containing chapter markdown files from one downloaded English translation

Its job is to update only the English translation sections of the verse blocks in the selected LuaLaTeX source files. It must copy the replacement English from the specified eng subfolder into the matching verse blocks and must preserve everything else: source attribution, Hebrew, commentary, spacing conventions, command names, comments, and final commentary blocks.

Do not use a loose regex over TeX. Parse balanced top-level verse commands so nested TeX inside English or commentary fields cannot confuse the edit. Start by inspecting the current top-level numbered book directories, beginning with 06-joshua, and identify the exact verse command shape before writing replacements.

The script should validate before writing:

  - every replacement verse has exactly one matching TeX verse block
  - every updated TeX verse has exactly one replacement English line
  - missing, duplicate, malformed, or unmatched references are reported clearly
  - the operation is deterministic

Prefer a dry-run mode by default or an explicit --check mode before writes, and provide a way to update a single file first so Joshua can be reviewed before applying the same mechanism to Judges, Samuel, Kings, Esther, and Ezra.
EOF
